        <tei:p><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n126.jpg" n="49"/><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/shacharit/repetition/gevurot/mekhalkel/text"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/gevurot/mekhalkel_chayyim">Sustaining life with kindness, reviving the dead with great compassion, supporting the falling, healing the sick and releasing the captives and keeping His faith with those who sleep in the dust. Who is like Thee, Master of might, and who resembles Thee, O King, who slays and revives and causes salvation to spring forth.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
